==Trivia==
*Unused sprites for this enemy were in the game as early as [[Version 4.2 Update|Version 4.2]], quite some time before his formal introduction in [[Version 5.5 Update|Version 5.5]]. However, he was named "Bloodsucker" and was visually just a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] palette swap of [[Master A.]]
*The "University of Yamaarashi" (ヤマアラシ大学) in his Japanese description may be a pun on the [[wikipedia:University of Yamanashi|University of Yamanashi]], with the joke being that ''Yamaarashi'' means porcupine (referencing his spiky appearance).
*In the Korean version, he's described as a sensual novelist who got popular through a book involving a girl's puberty titled "Love Through SNS" (사랑은 SNS로), became a professor in Nyanko University's Department of Korean Language and Literature, and is on the way to becoming a wizard, as in the Internet slang term "wizard" referring to a virgin over the age of 30.
*The [[Media:Ghost chapel splash jp 2.png|second Japanese event poster]] for [[01 The Ghost Chapel|#01 The Ghost Chapel]] reveals that [[Director Kurosawah]] directed a movie adaptation of Professor A.'s famous novel "Eguchi Kōkō" (江口高校, "Eguchi High School"), as well as "The Sleepless Peng" from [[Condemned Peng]]'s description.
**江口 ''Eguchi'' may be a play on how the kanji 口 ''guchi'' looks almost the same as the katakana syllable ロ ''ro''. If it were 江ロ, it would be pronounced like エロ ''ero'' (short for ''erotic''),
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!|The Battle Cats Unite]], this enemy is event-exclusive, being only located on [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 29|Floor 29]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]].

